  "summary": "I reviewed all 7 patients on \"DOAC dose review - week of 10/19/2026\" under RBC-PHARM-07. Final result: 4 doses changed and 3 left as they were. Each change has a progress note citing its sources.\n\nChanged:\n- pt-0061 Irene Castellano: apixaban raised from 2.5 to 5 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). She is 74, weighs 78 kg, SCr 1.02, so no dose criteria are met. The ID letter of 9/10 says she finished itraconazole on 8/14, so the interaction reduction no longer applies.\n- pt-0041 Raymond Duquette: apixaban lowered from 5 to 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0005). He meets no dose criteria, but he has an active itraconazole order (started 10/6). Itraconazole was not changed.\n- pt-0038 Eugene Moravec: rivaroxaban raised from 15 to 20 mg daily (mr-t0007). On his actual weight of 96 kg (age 79, SCr 1.45), CrCl is 56.1. The May reduction used ideal body weight, which the policy does not allow.\n  - A portal message this morning reports a home scale weight of 185 lb. A patient-reported weight is not a measured weight under the policy, so the dose stands. An addendum notes that if a clinic weight confirms about 84 kg, CrCl would be about 49 and he would need the 15 mg dose. Please get a measured weight at his next visit.\n- pt-0043 Marjorie Pellegrino: rivaroxaban lowered from 20 to 15 mg daily (mr-t0011). A new SCr of 1.25 (drawn 10/22) came in during the review; with age 75, female, 71 kg, CrCl is 43.6.\n\nUnchanged:\n- pt-0003 Frank Delgado: stays on rivaroxaban 20 mg daily. I first lowered him to 15 mg because the outside SCr was 160 µmol/L (CrCl 44.2). St. Brigid then corrected that result to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL) after an analyzer fault. CrCl is 59.9, so I put him back on 20 mg (mr-t0009) and wrote a correction note.\n- pt-0062 Norman Fairweather: stays on apixaban 5 mg twice daily. He meets only the age criterion (82). Two new ED creatinines arrived: 150 µmol/L on 10/21, then 100 µmol/L (1.13 mg/dL) on 10/22. The policy uses the most recent result, so the SCr criterion is not met.\n- pt-0002 Harold Vance: stays on apixaban 2.5 mg twice daily. I first raised him to 5 mg: he meets only the age criterion, and his weight (64.9 kg) and SCr (1.21) have recovered. Then a St. Brigid dermatology letter dated 10/22 arrived saying he started itraconazole that day for 12 weeks. That brings him back to 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0015), and I wrote a correction note.\n\nFollow-up:\n- Mr. Duquette's and Mr. Vance's apixaban doses should be reviewed again when their itraconazole courses end. For Mr. Vance that is about mid-January 2027.\n- No other medications were changed, including the itraconazole orders.\n\nInbox: I completed the 5 items that arrived during the review, with comments. The other items that were already in your results and message queues were not part of this list and are still open.",
